  "caption_latex": "Families E--G at $Jt=1$, plotted against separation $r$. {E and F each use forty trajectories per bath condition; G uses 22 for zero hopping and 21 for each nonzero hopping sign.} {(a--c)} {show} excitation-exchange family E: $C_{zz}$, $(C_{xx}+C_{yy})/2$ and staggered $C_{xy}$ from left to right. {(d--f)} {show} transverse-XXZ family F: $C_{zz}$, $C_{yy}$ and staggered $C_{xy}$. {(g--i)} {show} family G: $C_{xx}$, $C_{yy}$ and staggered $C_{yz}$. Every panel compares its family's bathless reference with zero, negative and positive bath hopping; E and F use $J_b=0,\\pm2J$, while G uses $J_b=0,\\pm J$. Bands are one standard error across the bath trajectories.",
